From 618cbdba52404f7b4107a510377da7f689e32513 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shogo Agent <agent@shogo.ai>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 06:07:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(static publish): emirate filter, district detail, honest
 predictions
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A static deployment (and any moment the API is down) renders from the baked
snapshot, and three things were wrong there:

- safeFetch fell back to one UNFILTERED register, so every emirate/search query
  returned the same full list and the map filter looked dead. Re-apply the
  server's where-clause over the baked rows (Dubai 32 / Abu Dhabi 12 / all 44).
- The district page used raw fetch().json(), which throws on the SPA shell the
  static host returns at 200 for /api/*, so it always rendered 'Community not
  found'. Route it through safeFetch and derive the single-district payload from
  the register.
- /predictions divided by a zero price, emitting NaN -> JSON null ('+null%') and
  falling through every branch of the momentum ladder to a fabricated 'Declining
  trend' for all 14 price-less districts. Forecast only where a price exists,
  bucket only measured districts, and render an em-dash.

build-snapshot.py also fetched /communities unauthenticated, which now returns
the 6-district guest teaser — a re-bake would have shrunk the published site
from 44 districts to 6. It uses the bootstrap session for that route now.

Meydan (+5.1%, no listings) no longer tops the gainers card.

Verified: day1 83, day2 30, fixes 41, stream 15, cron 31, intel 27, routing 8/8;
browser QA on the published host — 44/32/12/44 districts, Dubai Marina detail at
AED 2,265/sqft, predictions 25/3/2/30, no NaN/null in rendered text.

Co-authored-by: Shogo Agent <agent@shogo.ai>
