pfParse() read `property.size` straight into the Float column `areaSqft`, but
PropertyFinder returns that field as `{ value, unit }`. Every upsert threw
"Expected Float, provided Object" — 2,627 times in .shogo/logs/build.log — and the
same expression computed pricePerSqft as 0, since `object > 0` is false. The call
sat inside a bare `catch {}`, so the throw vanished, totalSaved stayed 0, and the
run was recorded as `success`.

scripts/scraper-pf.ts has handled both shapes since bdc193c, with a comment warning
about this exact error. This in-server copy is older (ceb358b) and never got the
same treatment: two copies of one parser, one of them fixed.

- pfParse accepts a number, a numeric string or { value }, and degrades to 0 rather
  than NaN — NaN fails the same Float check and would reproduce the outage.
- The listing loop counts saveFailures, keeps the first message, reports both in
  `logs` and the response, and records the run as `partial` with `errorMsg` set.
- Exported pfParse so the behaviour can be pinned by a test.

