Subject: [PATCH] fix(ui,api): a denial is not data, and a missing measurement
 is not a zero
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Closes every issue in the QA report on the deployed preview.

The headline defect was a privacy leak: the build-time snapshot is captured from
the demo session, and ACCOUNT-SCOPED endpoints were captured with it. Because
src/data/snapshot.json ships inside the public JS bundle, the deployed site served
the demo account's portfolio, watchlist, alert rules and identity to every visitor.
That is the [major] QA finding — a guest reading "Total Value AED 10,941,214" of
somebody else's holdings while /api/sqftlab/portfolio answered 403 — and it also
underlay both [minor] watchlist/alerts findings, where a 401 rendered as a working
empty state.

Account data no longer reaches the snapshot: the private paths are removed from
build-snapshot.py and a PRIVATE_PATHS guard refuses them even if re-added, the
snapshot was regenerated (16 keys, zero account-scoped, no trace of 10,941,214 /
"Demo Investor" / demo@sqftlab), and a runtime ACCOUNT_SCOPED denylist means
safeFetch can never resolve one from a stale copy.

Frontend
- loadResource/useResource report the HTTP status; AccessNotice turns 401 into a
  sign-in prompt, 403 into a plan prompt, and a network failure into a retry —
  never into placeholder figures. Portfolio, Watchlist, Alerts and Deals use it.
- Deals renders the explanation /deals already returned (insufficientData +
  message) instead of a blank page.
- Zeros that meant "unknown" now render as an em dash: the hero's hardcoded
  "585 transactions / 155 deals" fallback is gone, Markets shows "—" for
  transaction-derived figures with a note naming the cause, and no district shows
  "AED 0/sqft" (Meydan, Al Furjan).
- The hero's report strip was hardcoded sample data (including "47 DLD") sitting
  next to a "feed not connected" notice; it is now labelled an illustrative sample
  with transaction-derived cells as "—".
- Predictions district cards get accessible names; Pricing states that REST API
  keys are issued on request; the two listing counts are scoped (sale + rent vs
  sale-only); /favicon.ico 404 fixed with an SVG mark.

Backend
- /stats reports transactionSource + sources, so the client can tell "no
  transactions" from "no feed" instead of asserting zero.
- seededUserId() asked for demo@sqftlab.ae, which does not exist (the seed is
  .com), so it silently fell through to "oldest user" — correct only while the two
  are the same row. It now looks the demo addresses up explicitly.
- The limiter let cookie-less callers through: the guest middleware mints an id per
  request, so each got a fresh bucket (Remaining pinned at 19 across four anonymous
  requests, while cookie requests stepped 19→18→17→16). Keying on the client
  address is NOT safe here — measured through the edge, every visitor arrives as
  ::ffff:127.0.0.1 with no forwarding headers, so it would 429 the whole site. A
  client presenting a cookie keeps its per-visitor bucket; everything else shares a
  deliberate 600/min ceiling that no real browsing pattern reaches.

Verified: 307 checks across 10 suites green, tsc 0 errors outside src/generated,
build clean, and a browser QA run against the deployed preview confirming 8/8 —
Portfolio shows "Portfolio needs a Pro plan" with no monetary figures and no
occurrence of 10,941,214 anywhere in the rendered page.
