Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The kill switch stays OFF (PAYMENTS_ENABLED=false) and no keys are committed. What
this lands is the full code path, so activating it is a configuration change rather
than a development one.

src/lib/stripe.ts — deliberately LAZY. The brief's version built the client at
module scope and threw when STRIPE_SECRET_KEY was unset. custom-routes.ts imports
it, so that throw would have taken down the ENTIRE API in every environment with no
Stripe keys (dev, preview, CI), turning the kill switch — which exists so the site
runs without payments — into a boot crash. getStripe() returns null instead, and
the routes answer 503 listing exactly which env vars are missing.

Two more brief details simply do not compile against stripe@23:
  - `apiVersion: '2024-06-20'` is not in this SDK's types (it ships 2026-09-30.endive)
    and pinning an old version against a new SDK is a runtime hazard. Omitted.
  - `subscription.current_period_end` moved onto subscription ITEMS (API 2025-03-31).
    subscriptionPeriodEnd() reads it there, taking the latest boundary.
Also normaliseStripeStatus(): Stripe says `canceled`, the schema documents
`cancelled`; writing sub.status raw would put two spellings in one column.

Routes: POST /sqftlab/subscribe (kill switch -> 503 first, then 401, then 400 with
the field named, then a 503 naming missing config, never a 502 from a half-wired
account), a shared webhook handler on both /stripe/webhook and the existing
/webhooks/stripe, and GET /sqftlab/users/me with `entitled` mirroring the tier
middleware. A VERIFIED webhook event is still not applied while the switch is off,
so a delayed test event cannot start a subscription behind it. The sketch's
`process.env.NEXTAUTH_URL` is not a thing here — the checkout origin comes from
APP_URL or the request itself.

Pricing page at /pricing (the URL now selects it; the nav button alone left a shared
/pricing link on the landing page): four AED tiers, monthly/annual with the saving
computed, a 23-row comparison table, five FAQs. The paid CTAs do not fake a
redirect while the switch is off — they say so.

One honesty fix to the brief's copy: it asserts "Every plan includes live DLD
transaction data", and the DLD feed is NOT connected on this deployment. Claiming
it would sell a paying customer a source that does not exist — the same mistake the
About page already had to fix. The sentence now appears only once the feed is
genuinely connected; the trust strip reads /sqftlab/sources for the same reason.

Verified: 369 checks across 11 suites (49 new in verify-day5, including the
authenticated/invalid-plan branches driven in a child process with the flag flipped,
since they are unreachable while it is off); tsc clean outside src/generated; the
page renders on the deployed preview with all four tiers, the annual toggle and the
FAQ confirmed via a real browser.
