Enterprise-gated Comparable Market Analysis: value a unit from recorded sales of
comparable units, with the comparables returned so the user can check the working.

Task A — POST /sqftlab/cma (custom-routes.ts)
  * Auth before tier, so an anonymous caller gets 401 and a signed-in under-tier
    caller gets 403 with requiredTier/upgradeUrl. The brief's order (tier first)
    would answer 403 to a guest and imply a login alone unlocks an Enterprise tool.
  * The brief's Prisma query does not run against this schema: it asks for
    bedrooms/size/amount/floor/pricePsf/transactionType:'Sales' where the schema has
    beds/areaSqft/priceAed/floorNumber/pricePerSqft and lowercase
    sale|off_plan_sale|mortgage|gift. It also uses `mode:'insensitive'`, which the
    SQLite datasource rejects outright. Community resolution goes through the
    project's existing fuzzy matcher and the building match is done in JS, so the
    behaviour is identical on SQLite and on the PostgreSQL the brief targets.
  * Mortgage and gift rows are excluded: they are transactions but not arm's-length
    prices, and they would drag the median.
  * Same-building comps are preferred when >= 3 exist (tightest set, most defensible
    estimate); otherwise the community is used and compBasis says which.

Task B — src/components/CmaPage.tsx (route /cma)
  40/60 input form and results, mobile-first (stacks below lg). Enterprise gate with
  a blur overlay and an Upgrade CTA rather than an empty page. shadcn components as
  structure with this project's tokens applied via className/style, matching how
  PricingPage composes Table and Accordion — the app has no Tailwind @theme, so
  shadcn's own semantic utilities resolve to nothing.

Data honesty — the reason this tool cannot show a valuation on this deployment
  The transactions table is EMPTY here (0 rows); listings 7,553, communities 44. The
  DLD feed in src/lib/dld.ts needs DUBAI_PULSE_API_KEY, which is not set, and
  scripts/purge-mock-data.ts deliberately deletes the synthetic rows that
  seed-sqftlab.ts used to generate. So the route REFUSES (422, with compsFound and
  dldConnected) instead of substituting a community median — a valuation built on
  nothing is worse than no valuation, which is the platform's whole claim. The 422
  distinguishes three different causes so the message is actionable: sales exist but
  not for this query (widen the search), feed connected but nothing ingested yet, or
  no feed at all (name the missing credential).

Fixes found while verifying
  * src/vite-env.d.ts was missing. That single omission produced three unrelated
    `tsc --noEmit` errors (import.meta.env, and the CSS side-effect import), which is
    why "zero errors" was unreachable. Hand-written TS is now clean.
  * _env-guard pinned DATABASE_URL in only 3 of 10 suites; verify-day1..day3,
