Reuses computeCma instead of the brief snippet, whose query names fields this
schema does not have (area/bedrooms/size/amount/pricePsf) and passes
mode:insensitive, which the SQLite datasource rejects outright.

investmentScore is nullable in ReportData. The brief substituted 50 when no
score exists; this prints "Not yet computed" and the data coverage instead,
because on the finished page a placeholder is indistinguishable from a
measurement.

Every interpolated value is escaped, and the broker logo is restricted to an
inline base64 image — both land in a document Chromium renders, so unescaped
input is injection into the renderer rather than a cosmetic bug.

No remote webfont: the @import made every report depend on fonts.googleapis.com
answering, turning a slow font fetch into a failed export.

Chromium is resolved by probing (this host ships /usr/bin/chromium, not the
documented /usr/bin/chromium-browser), one instance is reused across renders,
concurrent renders are capped at 2, and the page closes in finally so a failed
export cannot leak a Chromium page per attempt.

A missing browser answers 503 with the reason; too few recorded sales answers
422 naming the missing credential. Neither is a 200 with a fabricated figure.

The button posts to /api/sqftlab/report/property — the brief omitted the /api
prefix, which would have 404ed — and renders the server message inline rather
than alert().

verify-day6 asserted the old "Coming soon" placeholder, so it would have failed
against the change Day 7 asks for; that assertion now covers the new wiring.
