Tasks A-D. The spec's code does not run against this codebase, so each part is
implemented against the real schema; the deviations are load-bearing.

PATH: server.tsx mounts this app with app.route('/api', customRoutes), so routes
are declared '/v1/...' and served at /api/v1/... . The spec's '/api/v1/...' would
have served /api/api/v1/... — every URL in its own docs 404s. Confirmed both ways
against the live server.

Task A — API keys
  · route already existed; added the per-tier cap (3/5/10/20) and 201 + the
    save-once warning.
  · FIX: keys were created with a hardcoded tier 'pro', so an institutional
    customer's allowance was enforced at 500/day instead of 100,000.
  · FIX: callsToday was only ever incremented and never reset, so a key that
    reached its limit once was permanently dead. Added calls_reset_at /
    month_reset_at and reset lazily on first use after the boundary, which also
    survives a scheduler outage or a mid-window restart.
  · FIX: the spec reads the owner's subscriptionStatus and never acts on it, so a
    cancelled customer's keys kept working. Now enforced.
  · API keys are read from the Authorization header only — a ?api_key= fallback
    writes live secrets into access logs.

Task B — /v1 endpoints
  · FIX: 'Sales' matches nothing (stored values are sale/off_plan_sale).
  · FIX: no area/bedrooms/size/pricePsf/amount column exists; the spec's filters
    and groupBy would not compile. Real columns are communityId/beds/areaSqft/
    pricePerSqft/priceAed.
  · FIX: mode:'insensitive' throws on SQLite — area text resolves via
    findCommunityByName instead.
  · an unmatched area returns 404 rather than silently exporting the whole table.

Task C — Export Centre
  · FIX: CSV had no escaping, so a community name containing a comma corrupted
    every subsequent column; embedded quotes were not doubled.
  · FIX: formula injection — scraping-supplied names beginning = + - @ executed
    in the buyer's spreadsheet. Guarded, with a numeric exemption so real
    negative values stay numeric.
  · FIX: 'unlimited' was implemented as take: 999999; rowLimitFor() now returns a
    documented ceiling and the response reports truncation honestly.
  · UTF-8 BOM so Excel reads Arabic names correctly; CRLF per RFC 4180.
  · xlsx installed from the SheetJS CDN: the npm line is frozen at 0.18.5 (2022)
    with two unpatched advisories, and the fixes were never published to npm.

Task D — Export Centre page
  · FIX: the spec polls /api/v1/transactions for the row count, but that endpoint
    is API-key authenticated and this page holds a session, so it would 401 for
    everyone. Counts come from a session-authed preview route.
  · Excel entitlement is answered by the server, not guessed client-side.

Also: scripts/fix-server-order.ts — the schema edit relocated the SHOGO:CUSTOM
block below the SPA catch-all again (routing 8/8 -> 1/8). A postgenerate hook was
tried and measured: it does NOT fire, because the in-editor regeneration calls the
SDK CLI directly. Repair is now one idempotent command.

Verified: 21 suites / 676 checks green, scripts/verify-day11.ts 76 checks,
0 hand-written TS errors, build clean, plus a live end-to-end pass against the
running server (key create -> v1 read -> export -> revoke).
