 breakdown
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Tasks A-E. DealAlert/AlertMatch and the alert engine already existed from earlier
days, so this reconciles against them rather than restructuring: the existing
design alerts on LISTINGS below a district's median PSF (a property you can still
buy), where the spec alerts on DLD transactions already completed. Kept.

Task A — schema
  · added `name` (the spec's user-given label) and `lastCheckedAt`. The latter is
    distinct from createdAt: an alert can sit for weeks without a match, and
    "checked 3m ago" is what answers "is the engine running?".

Task B — alert routes
  · added the per-plan cap the spec asks for (pro 5) with 403 + upgradeUrl. The
    spec's ladder again omits `elite` — it is a real tier ranking between pro and
    enterprise, so it sits at 25 rather than losing a paid feature.
  · "unlimited" (999999) replaced with a reported ceiling: the scan walks every
    active alert each run, so the count is a real cost.
  · GET now returns each alert's 3 newest matches plus limit/atLimit, so the list
    needs one request and the page reports the server's own allowance.
  · DELETE is now SOFT. It used to hard-delete and cascade the match history away
    with the rule — deleting a watch should not rewrite what it reported.

Task C — scan + notify: already wired into the hourly pipeline (more often than
  the spec's 6h). The scan now stamps lastCheckedAt on every evaluation, including
  the no-community / no-median path, since it did evaluate. Notify already refuses
  to mark an undelivered match as sent; the spec's updateMany({ notifiedAt: null })
  after a .catch(() => {}) erased alerts permanently on any send failure.

Task D — Investment Score
  · GAP: no endpoint ever returned a breakdown. Added GET /sqftlab/scores/:slug,
    gated server-side: the composite is public, the five weighted factors are
    withheld (not merely un-rendered) below Pro. The guest payload contains no
    factor key at all.
  · The spec's breakdown shape (psf/yield/momentum/neighbourhood/developer at
    25/25/20/15/15) is NOT the engine's (psfMomentum/rentalYield/supplyAbsorption/
    volumeTrend/capitalFlow at 30/25/20/15/10). Wiring it as written would have
    labelled supplyAbsorption "Neighbourhood" and the placeholder capitalFlow
    "Developer". Rebuilt to the engine's real factors.
  · Kept the descriptive bands (FIX-07): the spec's "Strong Buy Signal" is advice
    wording a composite score must not give.
  · Placeholder factors are greyed and marked n/a rather than drawn as a
    measurement, and are only sent when the breakdown is.

Task E — AlertsPage: added the name field, the "N/limit" banner from the server's
  count, and per-alert "Checked Xm ago". Note the page is gated to ELITE in the UI
  while the API now allows pro; flagged rather than silently flipped, since the
  ELITE badge and FeatureGate copy are the marketed positioning.

Verified: 22 suites / 698 checks green, verify-day12 61 checks, 0 hand-written TS
errors, build clean, plus a live pass (guest vs elite score payloads, named alert
create, soft delete).

Co-authored-by: Shogo Agent <agent@shogo.ai>
