dependency, so it would throw on construction. This pod carries AI_PROXY_TOKENS
(a projectId -> ai-proxy JWT map) which fronts Claude and answers
claude-haiku-4-5; the module uses that through the Shogo provider. Note the pod's
own RUNTIME_AUTH_SECRET is a workspace token (wrt_v1_) and the proxy rejects it.
With no credential the route answers 503 configured:false rather than inventing
an answer.

Quota: keyed on the identity the SERVER issued (account id, else the guest
cookie), not the brief's X-Session-Id header. A caller-supplied header can be
rotated per request, which would make "10 messages/day" unenforceable — the same
shape as the Day 4 limiter that gave every cookie-less client a fresh bucket. A
live check asserts a rotated header still returns 429. Two rows are written only
once a reply exists, so the counter can never exceed answers delivered, and a
failed call does not consume quota.

Prompt: history is rebuilt from validated turns (a caller-supplied `system` turn
is dropped) rather than taken on trust. With an empty register the prompt states
that outright and forbids quoting figures, instead of feeding the model
"0 transactions / AED 0" and inviting narration.

